<p class="lesson-lead">The first enemy that shoots. Distance checks, Instantiated projectiles, and the cooldown — the single most reused pattern of the year — all arrive in four lessons that end in a tuned, playtested threat.</p>

<h2>Lessons</h2>
<table>
    <tr><th>ID</th><th>Title</th><th>What you build / learn</th></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/3.1a.html">3.1a</a></td><td>The Turret: Distance &amp; the Detection Radius</td><td>Vector3.Distance as a region in space</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/3.2a.html">3.2a</a></td><td>Projectiles: Instantiate, Fire, Destroy</td><td>spawn, aim, rotate, travel, die</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/3.3a.html">3.3a</a></td><td>Fire Rate: Cooldowns &amp; Time</td><td>Time.time, lastAttackTime, the compound conditional</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="../../lessons/3.4a.html">3.4a</a></td><td>Turret Damage, Tuning &amp; Playtest</td><td>four difficulty knobs, three personalities, one fix</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Concepts this unit owns</h2>
<p>The <strong>cooldown/timestamp pattern</strong> is taught here and reused by enemy contact damage, your own swing, jump mercies, and turn gates. CED: AAP-1 (procedural abstraction: AttackPlayer hides the fire path), AAP-2 (calling procedures), AAP-3 (logic in compound conditionals).</p>

